{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019vgCA6snmBfJaEtDwj73io","type":"tool_result","content":"100\t- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3025):\n101\t  - Test 1 (`/tmp/playwright-test-us-047.js`): rendered the 3-item / 3-zone DragMatch; mouse-dragged i-var → z-fn (wrong) and i-fn → z-var (wrong) and i-loop → z-loop (right); clicked Submit → explanation Callout visible, `[data-misplaced=\"true\"]` on i-var/i-fn, `[data-misplaced=\"false\"]` on i-loop. Clicked Try again → reset → re-dragged into correct zones → Submit → button morphed to \"Solved\" and `[data-section-id=\"dm1\"] [data-status=\"done\"]` badge appeared. Screenshots at `/tmp/us-047-{1-initial,2-placed-wrong,3-after-wrong-submit,4-correct-placement,5-after-correct-submit,6-status-done}.png`.\n102\t  - Test 2 (`/tmp/playwright-test-us-047-keyboard.js`): focused i-var, pressed Space → `aria-pressed=true` (keyboard lift fired); pressed Space again → drop. Confirms `useSensor(KeyboardSensor)` is wired and `useDraggable` attached `role=button`, `tabIndex=0`, `aria-pressed`, `aria-roledescription=\"Draggable item\"`.\n103\t- **Assumptions made (no human in the loop):**\n104\t  - \"multipleItemsPerZone respected for ordering\" interpreted as: when `multipleItemsPerZone=true`, each zone's `accepts` array is matched with strict order; when `false`, set equality (so author can list multiple alternatives even if only one-at-a-time is allowed). Documented in `validateDragMatch` jsdoc-equivalent and exercised by both test cases.\n105\t  - \"subtle outline pointing back to expected zone\" rendered as a dashed danger-border outline + an inline italic \"→ <expected zone label>\" suffix on the misplaced item. Avoids drawing actual SVG arrows (would clash with dnd-kit's transform overlay) while still naming the destination.\n106\t  - When `multipleItemsPerZone=false` and the user drops a 2nd item on an already-occupied zone, the existing occupant is bounced back to the bank rather than rejecting the drop. Feels less surprising than a no-op for a single-user MVP.\n107\t- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n108\t  - dnd-kit listeners + `aria-pressed` toggle is the cheapest way to E2E-test keyboard accessibility — proving full keyboard navigation requires brittle ArrowKey/coords plumbing because the default `KeyboardCoordinateGetter` only translates by 25 px per press.\n109\t  - `useDraggable`'s `attributes` already include `aria-roledescription`; passing `attributes: { roleDescription: 'Draggable item' }` overrides only the localised string.\n110\t  - Style warning: do NOT mix shorthand `border` (in base style) with `borderColor` (in hover/feedback overrides). React logs a \"Removing borderColor\" warning on every re-render. Switch the base to longhand (`borderWidth`/`borderStyle`/`borderColor`) so hover only touches the longhand it overrides.\n111\t  - For widgets with auto-completion side-effects (PATCH /api/progress + onComplete), gate the call inside the click handler against a `useRef(false)` rather than a `useEffect`. The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` lint rule rejects `setState` in effects, but a ref flip + side-effect call inside the handler is both lint-clean and renders the same UX.\n112\t---\n113\t\n114\t## 2026-05-03 23:50 - US-046\n115\t- Implemented CodeCloze widget — fill-in-the-blank Python exercise with `{{slotId}}` placeholders, per-slot blur validation (exact / regex / oneOf), inline syntax-highlighted code, progressive hints driven by global failed-attempt count, and optional final pyodide-tested code assembly.\n116\t- Files added:\n117\t  - `src/widgets/CodeCloze/{schema.ts, sample.ts, CodeClozeWidget.tsx, CodeClozeEditor.tsx}`\n118\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/code-cloze.json` (regenerated)\n119\t  - `courses/cloze-test/{course.json, lessons/box-blur.json}` — smoke-test course\n120\t- Files changed:\n121\t  - `src/widgets/registry.ts` — `codeCloze` entry (PenLine icon, `--widget-code-cloze` accent), `WidgetType` union extended\n122\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` — added `code-cloze` to widget map\n123\t  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — `CodeClozeSectionSchema` variant added to discriminated union\n124\t  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — `--widget-code-cloze` CSS var in both `:root` (light) and dark blocks\n125\t  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — wired `CodeClozeEditor` into `WidgetEditPanel`, added `codeCloze` body branch in `SectionRenderer`, imported `ComponentType` (used to type the registry-fetched component when forwarding `progressKey`/`onComplete`)\n126\t  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — added discriminated-union case for `codeCloze` + dedicated `CodeClozeData` and `validateSlotValue` test blocks\n127\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated\n128\t- Quality checks: `npm run typecheck` clean (only pre-existing `pyodide` module errors in `src/lib/pyodide/{runner,stdout}.test.ts` — npm dev-dep isn't installed in this env, same on main). `npm test` passes 117 / skips 7 / fails only the same 2 pyodide test files. `npm run lint` introduces no new errors or warnings in `src/`.\n129\t- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3010):\n130\t  - Filled `aggregator` with wrong \"avg\" → slot turned red, inline `slot.hint` (\"Use the built-in that totals an iterable.\") appeared, and progressive hint #0 (revealAfterAttempts: 1) showed up.\n131\t  - Fixed to \"sum\" → green; filled `divisor` with \"len(values)\" → green.\n132\t  - Submit clicked once Pyodide reached `ready`; finalTests (2) passed in pyodide; submit button morphed to \"Solved\".\n133\t  - Server-side `GET /api/progress` confirmed `sectionState.c1.done === true`.\n134\t  - On reload, the section's `data-status=\"done\"` badge rendered. Screenshots at `/tmp/us-046-{1-initial,2-wrong,3-aggregator-fixed,4-passed}.png`.\n135\t- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n136\t  - Adding a new widget that runs Python via `runWithTests` does NOT need any worker-side wiring — the existing `runWithTests` already exec's user code in `__ai_lesson_globals` (per US-031) and runs each test body in `dict(__ai_lesson_globals)`, so test isolation is automatic. Just call `usePyodide().runWithTests(assembleCode(), tests)`.\n137\t  - For inline syntax-highlighted code WITH editable inputs interleaved, a regex-based Python tokenizer (keywords / strings / comments / numbers / fn-call detection) inside a `<pre>` is much simpler than a CodeMirror `Decoration.replace` widget — the input elements are React-managed and `onBlur` fires naturally without bridging into CodeMirror state. Trade-off: highlighting is less accurate than Lezer, but for the cloze use-case (small templates, ~50-200 chars) it is indistinguishable.\n138\t  - Inline `<input>` width auto-sizing: `width: calc(${ch}ch + 16px)` with `ch = max(value.length, 4)` keeps the input proportional to its content while honouring the 60px min from the AC. Avoid measuring DOM with refs — `ch` units already account for monospace glyph width.\n139\t  - The status badge selector for browser tests is `[data-section-id=\"<id>\"] [data-status=\"done\"]`, NOT `data-widget-status`. The `WidgetStatus` is rendered by `StatusBadge` as `data-status=\"done|progress\"`.\n140\t  - When persisting completion for non-Code widgets (no `userCode` to keep), PATCH `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { done: true } } }` — the server's `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges, so unrelated sibling fields (e.g. `userCode` from a Code widget on a different section) are unaffected since `sectionId` is per-instance.\n141\t---\n142\t\n143\t## 2026-05-03 22:25 - US-045\n144\t- Implemented ParametricExplorer widget — a generalised version of the Demo widget that injects sliders/select/toggle params as Python globals into a render code block, supports plot/value/both output, and debounces re-renders (default 150ms, configurable via `debounceMs`).\n145\t- Files added:\n146\t  - `src/widgets/ParametricExplorer/{schema.ts, sample.ts, ParametricExplorerWidget.tsx, ParametricExplorerEditor.tsx}`\n147\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/parametric-explorer.json` (regenerated)\n148\t  - `courses/pexp-test/{course.json, lessons/plot-mode.json, lessons/value-mode.json}` — smoke-test course\n149\t- Files changed:\n150\t  - `src/lib/pyodide/worker.ts` — new `runWithPlotParam` message + `__ai_pexp_run` Python helper; lazy matplotlib install with `AGG` backend; per-setupCode namespace cache (`__ai_pexp_namespaces[setup_code]`); captures most-recent figure as PNG and reads optional `result` global as JSON\n151\t  - `src/lib/pyodide/client.ts` — `runWithPlotParam` method + `RunWithPlotParamRequest`/`RunWithPlotParamResult` types added to `usePyodide()`\n152\t  - `src/widgets/registry.ts` — `parametricExplorer` entry (Sliders icon, `--widget-parametric-explorer` accent), WidgetType union extended\n153\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` — added `parametric-explorer` to widget map\n154\t  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — added `ParametricExplorerSectionSchema` variant to discriminated union\n155\t  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — new `--widget-parametric-explorer` CSS var in light + dark blocks\n156\t  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — wired `ParametricExplorerEditor` into `WidgetEditPanel` and the `parametricExplorer` body branch in `SectionRenderer`\n157\t  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — added schema tests (minimal-valid, select+toggle, debounceMs, unknown-outputType reject) and param-injection serialization tests (slider→number, toggle→bool, select→string, mixed)\n158\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated\n159\t- Quality checks: `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm test` 7 files / 116 tests pass, `npm run lint` only pre-existing errors in `claude/design/source/*.jsx` and `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/*.js` (no new errors in `src/`).\n160\t- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3008): plot-mode lesson dragged slider 1 → 4.5, plot redrew within debounce (verified by `<img>` src change); value-mode dragged 3 → 5, value text updated 9 → 25. Screenshots at `/tmp/us-045-{plot-initial,plot-after-drag,value-after-drag}.png`.\n161\t- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n162\t  - Pyodide takes a noticeable second (~2-5s) to lazy-install matplotlib on first `runWithPlotParam` — first plot blocks until install + setupCode + renderCode + figure savefig finish. Allow generous timeout in playwright (`waitForSelector('[data-testid=\"pexp-plot\"]', { timeout: 120_000 })`).\n163\t  - The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` rule catches `void asyncFn()` even when setState is post-await. Gate with a one-shot `useRef(false)` flag, which the rule treats as a one-time subscription pattern (mirrors GaussDemo's `pendingSigmaRef` gate).\n164\t  - When testing back-to-back lesson pages with Turbopack, the dev server can hang after one playwright run completes — `curl` to any route will then time out. Fix: kill the dev server and restart it on a different port between attempts.\n165\t---\n166\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb5c9adb-fc42-4b13-8a3c-82c2b6f512d6","uuid":"85aafd51-63d9-47f8-99fd-c82f65d47c35","timestamp":"2026-05-03T22:29:52.148Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-049/scripts/ralph/progress.txt","content":"- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3025):\n  - Test 1 (`/tmp/playwright-test-us-047.js`): rendered the 3-item / 3-zone DragMatch; mouse-dragged i-var → z-fn (wrong) and i-fn → z-var (wrong) and i-loop → z-loop (right); clicked Submit → explanation Callout visible, `[data-misplaced=\"true\"]` on i-var/i-fn, `[data-misplaced=\"false\"]` on i-loop. Clicked Try again → reset → re-dragged into correct zones → Submit → button morphed to \"Solved\" and `[data-section-id=\"dm1\"] [data-status=\"done\"]` badge appeared. Screenshots at `/tmp/us-047-{1-initial,2-placed-wrong,3-after-wrong-submit,4-correct-placeme