{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016RFr4x9a4H8dEC9v7TjrLZ","type":"tool_result","content":"42\t  - Cross-origin iframes (YouTube, Vimeo, etc.) prevent the parent from spying on or replacing methods on `iframe.contentWindow` — Chromium throws `SecurityError: Failed to set a named property 'postMessage' on 'Window': Blocked a frame with origin \"...\" from accessing a cross-origin frame`. For seek/play tests on third-party embeds, prefer observable side-effects (DOM state, our own component state) or test the seek path through MP4/HTML5 video where `currentTime` is observable from the parent.\n43\t  - Stubbing `<video>.currentTime` in playwright: `Object.defineProperty(v, 'currentTime', { get, set, configurable: true })` works AFTER the React component has done its initial assignment. To verify both an initial `startAt` assignment AND subsequent click-driven seeks, READ `video.currentTime` first (captures the post-mount value), THEN install the descriptor override (captures subsequent writes). If you override before the initial currentTime read, the underlying setter's effect on the native element is lost.\n44\t  - Asset API extension: adding new media types to `src/app/api/courses/[slug]/assets/[...path]/route.ts` is a one-line change (extend `CONTENT_TYPES`). The same map gates BOTH the GET Content-Type header and the PUT extension allow-list, so adding `.mp4` lets video assets be served with the correct mime type and uploaded via the existing PUT endpoint.\n45\t  - For the YouTube iframe API without loading `youtube/iframe_api`: send raw `{event:'command', func, args}` JSON strings via `iframe.contentWindow.postMessage(..., '*')`. To receive `currentTime`, listen for `message` events from the iframe and parse `{event:'infoDelivery', info:{currentTime}}` payloads. Activate this stream with `addEventListener('onStateChange')` after the iframe fires `onReady`.\n46\t  - `extractYouTubeId` regex `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{11}$` covers all current YouTube IDs but also matches a sample text like `aircAruvnKk` — that's intentional for \"paste either the URL or the ID\" UX. URLs are handled by the `URL()` constructor with explicit host allow-listing (`youtube.com`, `m.youtube.com`, `youtu.be`, `youtube-nocookie.com`).\n47\t\n48\t## Codebase Patterns\n49\t- Cross-origin iframe (YouTube, Vimeo, etc.) postMessage spying from a playwright test is BLOCKED by Chromium (`SecurityError: Blocked a frame with origin \"...\" from accessing a cross-origin frame`). For seek/play verification on third-party video embeds, prefer either (a) observable side-effects in the parent's DOM/state, or (b) routing the test through an HTML5 `<video>` MP4 path where `video.currentTime` IS reachable from the parent and `Object.defineProperty(v, 'currentTime', {...})` works.\n50\t- Adding a new media type to course assets = extend `CONTENT_TYPES` in `src/app/api/courses/[slug]/assets/[...path]/route.ts` (one map gates both the GET Content-Type header and the PUT extension allow-list). Currently supports `.png/.jpg/.jpeg/.svg/.webp/.gif/.mp4/.webm`.\n51\t\n52\t## 2026-05-04 00:30 - US-048\n53\t- Implemented DataTable widget — sortable / filterable / paginated table for inline datasets, results, and comparisons. Click a column header to cycle asc → desc → unsorted (stable, original order preserved). Per-filterable-column filter row: text-contains for `string`, paired min/max number inputs for `number`. Pagination centred below the table (Prev / \"Page X of Y\" / Next) appears only when `rows.length > pageSize`. Numeric cells use `toLocaleString()` for thousand separators; boolean cells render as `✓`/`—`. Sticky `<thead>` inside an `overflow:auto` scroll wrapper (max-height 60vh) so headers stay visible when scrolling many rows.\n54\t- Files added:\n55\t  - `src/widgets/DataTable/{schema.ts, sample.ts, DataTableWidget.tsx, DataTableEditor.tsx}`\n56\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/data-table.json` (regenerated by `npm run build:schemas`)\n57\t  - `courses/datatable-test/{course.json, lessons/scores.json}` — smoke-test course (30 rows × 4 cols, pageSize 10)\n58\t- Files changed:\n59\t  - `src/widgets/registry.ts` — `dataTable` entry (Table icon from lucide-react, `--widget-data-table` accent), `WidgetType` union extended\n60\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` — added `data-table` to widgets map\n61\t  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — `DataTableSectionSchema` variant added to discriminated union\n62\t  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — `--widget-data-table` CSS var in both light (`#4a6f8a`) + dark (`#94b3d0`) blocks\n63\t  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — wired `DataTableEditor` into `WidgetEditPanel` and added `dataTable` body branch in `SectionRenderer`\n64\t  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — discriminated-union case for `dataTable` + dedicated `DataTableData` schema tests, `sortRows` tests (asc/desc/unsorted/null-handling/non-mutating), `filterRows` tests (string contains, number range, AND of multiple filters, ignores non-filterable columns, empty filters pass-through)\n65\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated\n66\t  - `scripts/ralph/progress.txt` — added 2 codebase patterns (clampedPage instead of setState-in-effect, sticky-thead recipe)\n67\t- Quality checks: `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm test` 7 files / 155 tests pass (added 19 new tests over US-047), `npm run lint` clean in `src/widgets/DataTable/` (only pre-existing errors remain in `claude/design/source/*.jsx` and `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/*.js`).\n68\t- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3036/courses/datatable-test/lessons/scores, `/tmp/playwright-test-us-048.js`):\n69\t  - Loaded 30-row × 4-col table, pageSize=10 → \"Page 1 of 3\" indicator visible.\n70\t  - Clicked Score header → ascending sort verified (every cell ≥ previous on page 1: 20,21,23,25,26,28,30,31,33,35).\n71\t  - Clicked again → descending sort verified (69,67,65,64,62,60,59,57,55,54).\n72\t  - Clicked third time → header `data-sort` attribute reverts to `none` (insertion order restored).\n73\t  - Filtered Name column with \"gra\" → summary shows \"Showing 1–1 of 1 (filtered from 30)\", only \"Grace\" visible.\n74\t  - Cleared filter, set Score min=70 → empty state (\"No matching rows\") since sample scores top out at 69, confirming range filter applies.\n75\t  - Clicked Next → \"Page 2 of 3\", row indices start at 10 (verified `[data-testid=\"datatable-cell-10-name\"]` exists), boolean cells render `✓`/`—`. Clicked Prev → returned to Page 1.\n76\t  - Screenshots at `/tmp/us-048-{1-initial,2-sorted-desc,3-filtered,4-numfiltered,5-page2}.png`.\n77\t- **Assumptions made (no human in the loop):**\n78\t  - \"Sort indicator chevron shown next to header label\" — used `ChevronUp`/`ChevronDown` for active asc/desc and a dimmed `ChevronsUpDown` for sortable-but-unsorted columns. Non-sortable columns render as plain `<span>` with no chevron and no button.\n79\t  - \"Numeric columns formatted via `toLocaleString()`\" applied to the user-facing cell rendering only — the underlying row data and sort comparisons use the raw numeric value, so locale-formatted strings like `1,000` don't break `min/max` filter parsing.\n80\t  - Number range filter: blank min OR blank max means \"no bound on that side\"; setting both to blank disables the column filter entirely.\n81\t  - Boolean column filter: AC says \"filter input per filterable column (text contains for string type, range min/max inputs for number type)\" — boolean has no described filter UI, so `filterable: true` on a boolean column degrades gracefully (the column simply renders no filter input). Sample course marks the boolean column `filterable: false` to avoid surprise.\n82\t- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n83\t  - The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` rule fires even when the setState is a clamping no-op like `if (page >= totalPages) setPage(totalPages-1)`. Cheaper fix than a one-shot ref: derive a `clampedPage` purely at render time and use it everywhere (slicing, indicator text, disabled-state). Saves a render cycle and silences the rule.\n84\t  - Sticky `<thead>` works out-of-the-box with `position: sticky; top: 0` if (a) the scroll context is a wrapping `div` with `overflow: auto` and `maxHeight`, and (b) every `<th>` (or the `<thead>` itself) has an opaque `background`. Without (b), rows scroll *through* the header instead of *behind* it.\n85\t  - For widgets that own non-trivial pure logic (sort, filter, validation), export the helpers from the schema file alongside the Zod schema so vitest can unit-test them without rendering React. `validateDragMatch` (US-047) and `sortRows`/`filterRows` (US-048) follow this pattern — keeps `schemas.test.ts` as the single test file for \"pure data\" behaviour.\n86\t---\n87\t\n88\t\n89\t## Codebase Patterns\n90\t- Repo dir is named `US-001` (capitalized) → cannot run `create-next-app .` directly because npm rejects capital letters in package names. Workaround: scaffold into a temp dir (e.g. `/tmp/ai-lecturer-scaffold`), then copy files into the worktree (skip the inner `.git`), and set the package name in `package.json` manually.\n91\t- `shadcn@latest` (v4.x) emits Tailwind v4 / `base-nova` style by default — incompatible with a Tailwind v3 project. Use `shadcn@2.3.0` for v3-compatible init, or write `components.json` by hand.\n92\t- Tailwind v3 baseline = `@tailwind base; @tailwind components; @tailwind utilities;` in `globals.css` + `tailwind.config.ts` with `content: [\"./src/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,mdx}\"]` + `postcss.config.js` with `tailwindcss` and `autoprefixer` plugins. Theme/token wiring belongs in US-002, not US-001.\n93\t- Design tokens live in `src/styles/tokens.css` (canonical source from `claude/design/source/tokens.css`) and are imported at the top of `src/app/globals.css`. Tailwind utilities resolve through CSS vars, so changing a `--*` value at runtime updates Tailwind classes too.\n94\t- Theme/accent/density are switched by `data-theme` / `data-accent` / `data-density` attributes on `<html>` (defaults: `light` / `default` / `comfortable`). Selectors in tokens.css are scoped to `:root[data-theme=…]` etc. — adding new variants means adding a new `:root[data-…=\"…\"]` block, not a new file.\n95\t- Geist Sans + Mono are loaded via `next/font` (`geist/font/sans`, `geist/font/mono`) in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Their `.variable` classNames define `--font-geist-sans` / `--font-geist-mono`; tokens.css references those via `var(--font-geist-sans)` inside `--font-sans` / `--font-prose` / `--font-display`. Don't hardcode font names anywhere else.\n96\t- Playwright skill at `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/` ships without `node_modules`; run `npm install --no-audit --no-fund` inside it before first use. Its `detectDevServers()` helper missed our :3000 dev server even when up — fall back to setting `TARGET_URL` manually in the test script if detection fails.\n97\t- **Zod is pinned to v3** (`^3.25.x`) because `zod-to-json-schema` returns an empty object on Zod v4. Don't bump zod to v4 unless the `zod-to-json-schema` import also changes. (Zod v4 has a native `z.toJSONSchema()`, but our AC mandates the third-party lib.)\n98\t- **Vitest needs its own alias config.** `vitest.config.ts` must declare `resolve.alias = { '@': fileURLToPath(new URL('./src', import.meta.url)) }`. Vitest does NOT read `tsconfig.json#paths`. Next + `tsc` + `tsx` (used by `npm run build:schemas`) DO auto-pick it up.\n99\t- **Eslint config does not exempt `_`-prefixed unused vars.** For \"drop one field\" test fixtures, use `const broken: Partial<typeof obj> = { ...obj }; delete broken.field;` — destructuring with `_name` triggers `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` warnings.\n100\t- **Schema layout.** Source-of-truth Zod schemas live in two places: per-widget data shapes at `src/widgets/<Name>/schema.ts`; everything else (Course, Module, Lesson, Section discriminated union, Progress, CourseSpec) at `src/lib/schemas/`. `SectionSchema` is a `z.discriminatedUnion('type', […])` over `'theory'|'quiz'|'code'|'demo'|'sandbox'|'custom'`. Adding a new widget = new folder under `src/widgets/<Name>/` + register a variant in `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` + add it to the `widgets` map in `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts`. `npm run build:schemas` regenerates the committed `*.json` files in `src/widgets/schemas/`.\n101\t- **Filesystem helpers** live in `src/lib/server/` (server-only — never import from a `'use client'` module). `paths.ts` exports `coursesRoot()`, `assertSafeSlug()`, `slugify()`, `courseDir/courseFile/courseSpecFile/lessonFile()`. `atomic.ts` exports `atomicWriteJson(path, data)` (writes to `<path>.tmp` then `fs.rename`). `coursesRoot()` honours `COURSES_ROOT_OVERRIDE` env var (used in tests); production reads `path.join(process.cwd(), 'courses')`. Disk layout: `courses/<slug>/{course.json, course-spec.json, lessons/<lessonSlug>.json}`.\n102\t- **Next 16 route handlers + vitest.** Tests can import handlers directly from `src/app/api/.../route.ts` and call them with a synthesised `Request` and `{ params: Promise.resolve({...}) }` (Next 15+ wraps params in a Promise). `NextResponse.json()` returns a real `Response`, so `await res.json()` and `res.status` work in tests. Put the test file OUTSIDE `src/app/` (e.g. `src/lib/server/api.test.ts`) so Next doesn't try to compile it as a route — vitest's `include: 'src/**/*.test.ts'` still picks it up.\n103\t- **Slug rules.** `assertSafeSlug` rejects empty strings and any slug containing `/`, `\\`, or `..` (path-traversal protection). Public slugs are derived from user input via `slugify()` (NFKD-normalise → strip combining marks → lowercase → `[_\\s]+→-` → strip non-`[a-z0-9-]` → collapse `-+` → trim). Slugify can return `''` for all-punctuation inputs; callers must guard (POST `/api/courses` returns 400 in that case).\n104\t- **Pyodide worker singleton.** Web Workers are bundled by Turbopack via `new Worker(new URL('./worker.ts', import.meta.url))` (NO `type: 'module'` → classic worker, can use `importScripts` for CDN bootstrap). The worker file at `src/lib/pyodide/worker.ts` is excluded from main thread imports by virtue of being instantiated only via the URL constructor. Client hook lives at `src/lib/pyodide/client.ts` (`'use client'`) and exposes `usePyodide()`; the worker is a module-scope singleton created lazily on first hook subscription via `useSyncExternalStore`. Subscription on mount = lazy-load contract: dashboards / SSR never trigger worker creation. For id-keyed promise resolution: each `run`/`runWithTests` call generates `req-N`, stores `{resolve, reject}` in a `Map`, and pops on matching `event.data.id`. Custom test runner (no pytest) lives in a Python `__ai_run_tests` function injected once per worker; it `exec()`s each test body in a fresh copy of the user namespace and catches `AssertionError` separately for `assertionDetail`. Test results array shape: `[{name, passed, traceback?, assertionDetail?}]`.\n105\t- **CodeMirror 6 setup.** Packages: `codemirror @codemirror/state @codemirror/view @codemirror/lang-python @codemirror/commands @codemirror/language @codemirror/autocomplete` (commands brings `defaultKeymap`/`history`/`historyKeymap`/`indentWithTab`; language brings `HighlightStyle`/`syntaxHighlighting`/`bracketMatching`/`indentOnInput`). Theme via `EditorView.theme({...})` consuming our `--code-bg/--code-text/--code-keyword/...` CSS vars. Highlight via `HighlightStyle.define([{ tag: t.keyword, color: 'var(--code-keyword)' }, ...])` from `@lezer/highlight` tags. Editor instantiated once in `useEffect(() => {...}, [])` with `EditorState.create({doc, extensions:[…]})`; subsequent doc updates flow via `view.dispatch({changes:{from,to,insert}})`, NOT by re-rendering. Use `EditorView.updateListener.of((u)=>u.docChanged && setCode(u.state.doc.toString()))` to mirror doc into React state.\n106\t- **eslint react-hooks/refs rule is strict.** Never write `someRef.current = value` at component top level — must be inside `useEffect(() => { someRef.current = value; }, [value])` or inside an event handler. Pattern for \"always-fresh closure\" inside a handler set up once: declare `const valueRef = useRef(value); useEffect(() => { valueRef.current = value; }, [value]);` then read `valueRef.current` inside the long-lived closure.\n107\t- **Cmd/Ctrl+Enter in CodeMirror.** Use `keymap.of([{ key: 'Mod-Enter', preventDefault: true, run: () => { ...; return true; } }])` and put it BEFORE the `defaultKeymap` keymap so it wins over Cm-Enter defaults. `Mod` resolves to ⌘ on Mac and Ctrl elsewhere. Have the `run` callback dispatch via a ref (`handleRunRef.current()`) so it always picks up the latest closure.\n108\t- **Progress PATCH for sectionState.** PATCH `/api/progress` with body `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { userCode } } }`. To CLEAR a section's state (e.g. on Reset), send `{ [sectionId]: {} }` — the server's `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges into existing `sectionState[sectionId]` then replaces it, so `{}` overwrites and effectively wipes the entry's userCode. Caveat: this also wipes any sibling fields (quizSubmission) on the same section, which is fine because section IDs are per-widget-instance. To mark a section \"done\", PATCH `{ userCode, done: true }` together — `done?: boolean` is the per-section completion flag (added in US-011); sending `{ done: true }` alone would wipe userCode.\n109\t- **CodeRunner slots (US-011).** CodeRunner exposes slot props for graded variants without re-implementing the editor/footer: `extraPanel?: ReactNode` (rendered between output panel and footer), `primaryAction?: { label, icon, onClick, disabled, variant: 'primary'|'secondary'|'ghost', testId, ariaLabel }` (replaces ▶ Run; pass `null` to hide it entirely), `onCodeChange?: (code) => void` (mirror doc into parent state), `onReset?: () => void` (parent can also reset its own state when CodeRunner's Reset fires), `outputPlaceholder?: string`. CodeRunner also exports `codeRunnerEditorTheme` and `codeRunnerHighlightStyle` so child components (e.g. inline read-only test bodies) match the editor's look. Read-only CodeMirror needs BOTH `EditorState.readOnly.of(true)` and `EditorView.editable.of(false)`.\n110\t- **TS target ES2017.** The regex `s` (dotAll) flag triggers `TS1501`. Use `[\\s\\S]` in patterns that need to span newlines, never `/.../s`.\n111\t- **Lesson navigation.** Flat ordered lesson list = `course.modules.flatMap(m => m.lessons)`. Prev/next of current lesson is index-1 / index+1 in that list, crossing module boundaries. Client navigation uses `router.push(\\`/courses/\\${slug}/lessons/\\${targetSlug}\\`)` from `next/navigation`'s `useRouter()`. Mark-finished is `PATCH /api/progress { courseSlug, lessonSlug, status: 'finished' }` — applyProgressPatch already handles this and stamps `finishedAt`.\n112\t- **Adding a new widget type = 5 mandatory wiring points** (see `src/widgets/README.md`): (1) `--widget-<name>` CSS var in both light + dark blocks of `src/styles/tokens.css`; (2) Zod data schema at `src/widgets/<Name>/schema.ts` + register in `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` so `npm run build:schemas` emits `<name>.json`; (3) `widgetRegistry` entry in `src/widgets/registry.ts` (component / label / icon / accentVar) + extend the `WidgetType` union; (4) `<Name>Editor.tsx` per US-023 pattern + import + branch in both `WidgetEditPanel` and `SectionRenderer` in `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx`; (5) `<Name>SectionSchema` variant in `SectionSchema` discriminated union at `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts`. Skipping (5) means widget renders but lesson JSON containing it fails API validation. Histogram (US-030) is the canonical reference implementation.\n113\t- **React-aware playwright slider input.** Setting `el.value` directly bypasses React's value tracker — the `onChange` handler sees the *previous* value. Use the native setter override: `Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(window.HTMLInputElement.prototype, 'value').set.call(el, '4'); el.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));`. Same pattern works for `<select>`, `<textarea>`.\n114\t- **Pyodide lesson namespace + test isolation (US-031).** Worker holds a Python-side module-level dict `__ai_lesson_globals` (sourced from `src/lib/pyodide/runnerPython.ts` so vitest can re-install it via the `pyodide` npm dev-dep). All `'run'` calls exec'd with `runPythonAsync(code, { globals: lessonGlobalsProxy })` so the namespace persists across Code/Sandbox widgets within a lesson; `'runWithTests'` exec's user code in lessonGlobals (so helpers persist) but each test body in `dict(__ai_lesson_globals)` (so test mutations don't leak). `'resetNamespace'` (new message type, payload `{ lessonSlug }`) calls `__ai_reset_namespace()` which `.clear()`s in place — DON'T reassign the dict, the JS-side proxy points at the original object. Lesson page calls `usePyodide().resetNamespace(lessonSlug)` from a `useEffect([lessonSlug])` so the namespace wipes on every lesson navigation; toolbar `[data-testid=\"reset-session-btn\"]` exposes a manual reset with a `[data-testid=\"session-toast\"]` ack.\n115\t- **Browser tests touching Code/Sandbox widgets must clear `~/.ai-lecturer/progress.json` per-section state first.** Persisted `userCode` (from US-011) auto-loads as `initialCode`, so a stale entry from a prior aborted run silently shapes Submit outcomes. Wipe via `node -e` JSON edit or use a throwaway course slug.\n116\t- **CodeMirror typing in playwright auto-indents on `\\n`.** `keyboard.type('def f():\\\\n    return 42\\\\n')` produces compound indents. Use single-line lambdas where possible; otherwise insert `Enter` + `Home` between lines, or paste via `view.dispatch({changes:{...}})`.\n117\t- **Pyodide batched stdout strips `\\n` (US-032).** `setStdout({ batched })` fires once per line, content only — never join chunks with `''` or consecutive `print()`s collapse into one line. Use the `formatStdoutChunks` helper at `src/lib/pyodide/stdout.ts`: joins with `\\n`, then per-line keeps only the substring after the last `\\r` so terminal-style in-place updates work and bare `\\r`s don't render as extra line breaks under `pre-wrap`. The CodeRunner output panel already uses `whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap'`, so once newlines actually exist in the text, multi-line output renders correctly.\n118\t- **Worker plot capture (US-045 `runWithPlotParam`).** Matplotlib loaded lazily on first request via `loadPackage(['matplotlib'])` then `matplotlib.use('AGG')` (no display server in worker). Cache namespaces by `setupCode` STRING as the key (`__ai_pexp_namespaces[setup_code]`) so identical setupCode runs once per session — the cached dict is copied with `dict(cached)` for each render so user mutations don't leak. Capture the most-recent figure with `plt.figure(plt.get_fignums()[-1]).savefig(buf, format='png', bbox_inches='tight', dpi=110)` then `plt.close('all')` before the next render. JS plain-object payload (`{name: number|string|boolean}`) crosses the JS→Py boundary as a JsProxy → `params.to_py()` yields a Python dict; types are preserved automatically (number→float, bool→bool, string→str).\n119\t- **Next dev (Turbopack) can hang under back-to-back playwright runs.** Symptom: first navigation succeeds, second test run's `page.goto` times out and `curl` to ANY route hangs indefinitely. Recovery: `pkill -f \"next dev\"` and restart on a different port. Suspect dangling chromium HMR socket from the previous run.\n120\t- **react-hooks/set-state-in-effect rule.** A bare `void asyncFn()` inside `useEffect` triggers this even if setState happens after `await` (the linter doesn't follow async boundaries). Gate the call behind a one-shot `useRef(false)` flag (`if (initialRenderRef.current) return; initialRenderRef.current = true; void asyncFn();`) — the linter sees this as a one-time subscription and accepts it. Same gating pattern that GaussDemo uses with its `pendingSigmaRef` ref-check.\n121\t- **Mark a non-Code section \"done\".** PATCH `/api/progress` with `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { done: true } } }`. `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges into `sectionState[sectionId]`, so sibling fields on other sections are untouched. Section IDs are per-widget-instance, so this is the canonical pattern when there's no `userCode` to persist (Quiz, CodeCloze, DragMatch, etc.).\n122\t- **Mixing CSS shorthand `border` with separate `borderColor` re-renders trigger a React style warning.** Don't compose `{ border: '1px solid X' }` with a hover override `{ borderColor: 'Y' }`. Use longhand from the start (`borderWidth`, `borderStyle`, `borderColor`) so hover/feedback states only override the longhand piece. Surfaces this in DragMatch zone/bank styles where hover swaps the colour.\n123\t- **dnd-kit (`@dnd-kit/core` + `@dnd-kit/sortable`) is already in `package.json` (added pre-MVP).** `useSensors(useSensor(PointerSensor, { activationConstraint: { distance: 4 } }), useSensor(KeyboardSensor))` is the canonical sensor set for keyboard-accessible drag widgets. `useDraggable` automatically attaches `role=\"button\"`, `tabIndex=0`, `aria-pressed`, `aria-roledescription` — verifying those attributes is enough to prove keyboard sensors are wired without simulating arrow-key navigation in playwright (each ArrowKey only moves 25 px by default and the simulated drag is brittle). For a draggable+droppable bank/zone layout: track `placement: Record<containerId, itemId[]>` with a sentinel `__bank__` id; on `onDragEnd` find the item's source container, splice it out, push into the target. Use `<DragOverlay>` so the drag preview is portal-rendered and unaffected by transforms inside the original layout.\n124\t- **Inline syntax-highlight for cloze-style widgets.** Don't pull in CodeMirror with `Decoration.replace` widgets when the only requirement is \"syntax-highlighted Python with inline editable inputs\" — a small regex-based tokenizer (keywords / strings / comments / numbers / fn-call) inside `<pre>` is enough, and React-managed `<input>`s blur naturally without bridging CM state. CodeCloze's `tokenizePython` is the reference implementation. Use CodeMirror only when the user types into the code itself (Code, Sandbox, ParametricExplorer's Python editors).\n125\t- **Status badge selector for browser tests.** `[data-section-id=\"<id>\"] [data-status=\"done\"]` (NOT `data-widget-status`). `StatusBadge` in `src/widgets/Widget.tsx` exposes the value via `data-status`.\n126\t- **`type ComponentType` import for `widgetRegistry[type].component`.** When the lesson page's `SectionRenderer` forwards optional widget-specific props (e.g. `progressKey`, `onComplete`) via the registry, narrow the registry's `ComponentType<{ data?: unknown }>` with a local cast: `widgetRegistry.codeCloze.component as ComponentType<{ data?: unknown; progressKey?: typeof progressKey; onComplete?: () => void }>`. Add `type ComponentType` to the existing `from 'react'` import block in `page.tsx`.\n127\t- **Avoid `useEffect`+`setState` for \"clamp paging index when filter shrinks rows\".** The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` rule rejects `useEffect(() => setPage(Math.max(0, totalPages-1)))`. Instead, derive a `clampedPage = Math.min(page, totalPages-1)` value during render and use it for slicing/indicator/disabled-state — let `setPage` only flip on actual user click. This keeps the linter happy and removes a redundant render cycle when filters narrow the result set.\n128\t- **Sticky thead inside an `overflow:auto` scroll container.** `position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 1` on `<thead>` plus a non-transparent `background` on each `<th>` (or on the `<thead>` itself) is enough — no JS needed. Wrap the `<table>` in a `div` with `maxHeight: '60vh'; overflow: auto` so the sticky context is the wrapper rather than the page.\n129\t\n130\t## 2026-05-04 00:15 - US-047\n131\t- Implemented DragMatch widget — drag-and-drop matching for term↔definition / category↔example / label↔diagram. Items live in a top \"bank\" droppable; zones below accept items, optionally multiple per zone with order checked. Submit highlights correct zones (--success-border + --success-subtle) and incorrect zones (--danger-border + --danger-subtle); misplaced items get a dashed danger outline plus an italic \"→ <expected zone label>\" label pointing them home. Explanation rendered below the answer area as a neutral-tone Callout (info) per the Quiz widget pattern. Section auto-marks `done` on first all-correct submission via `PATCH /api/progress`.\n132\t- Files added:\n133\t  - `src/widgets/DragMatch/{schema.ts, sample.ts, DragMatchWidget.tsx, DragMatchEditor.tsx}`\n134\t  - `src/widgets/schemas/drag-match.json` (regenerated)\n135\t  - `courses/dragmatch-test/{course.json, lessons/terms.json}` — smoke-test course\n136\t- Files changed:"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb5c9adb-fc42-4b13-8a3c-82c2b6f512d6","uuid":"302b7201-2bd5-4284-89f3-df3265bbaf64","timestamp":"2026-05-03T22:41:50.879Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-049/scripts/ralph/progress.txt","content":"  - Cross-origin iframes (YouTube, Vimeo, etc.) prevent the parent from spying on or replacing methods on `iframe.contentWindow` — Chromium throws `SecurityError: Failed to set a named property 'postMessage' on 'Window': Blocked a frame with origin \"...\" from accessing a cross-origin frame`. For seek/play tests on third-party embeds, prefer observable side-effects (DOM state, our own component state) or test the seek path through MP4/HTML5 video where `currentTime` is observable from the parent.\n  - Stubbing `<video>.currentTime` in playwright: `Object.defineProperty(v, 'currentTime', { get, set, configurable: true })` works AFTER the React component has done its initial assignment. To verify both an initial `startAt` assignment AND subsequent click-driven seeks, READ `video.currentTime` first (captures the post-mount value), THEN install the descriptor override (captures subsequent writes). If you override before the initial currentTime read, the underlying setter's effect on the native element is lost.\n  - Asset API extension: adding new media types to `src/app/api/courses/[slug]/assets/[...path]/route.ts` is a one-line change (extend `CONTENT_TYPES`). The same map gates BOTH the GET Content-Type header and the PUT extension allow-list, so adding `.mp4` lets video assets be served with the correct mime type and uploaded via the existing PUT endpoint.\n  - For the YouTube iframe API without loading `youtube/iframe_api`: send raw `{event:'command', func, args}` JSON strings via `iframe.contentWindow.postMessage(..., '*')`. To receive `currentTime`, listen for `message` events from the iframe and parse `{event:'infoDelivery', info:{currentTime}}` payloads. Activate this stream with `addEventListener('onStateChange')` after the iframe fires `onReady`.\n  - `extractYouTubeId` regex `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{11}$` covers all current YouTube IDs but also matches a sample text like `aircAruvnKk` — that's intentional for \"paste either the URL or the ID\" UX. URLs are handled by the `URL()` constructor with explicit host allow-listing (`youtube.com`, `m.youtube.com`, `youtu.be`, `youtube-nocookie.com`).\n\n## Codebase Patterns\n- Cross-origin iframe (YouTube, Vimeo, etc.) postMessage spying from a playwright test is BLOCKED by Chromium (`SecurityError: Blocked a frame with origin \"...\" from accessing a cross-origin frame`). For seek/play verification on third-party video embeds, prefer either (a) observable side-effects in the parent's DOM/state, or (b) routing the test through an HTML5 `<video>` MP4 path where `video.currentTime` IS reachable from the parent and `Object.defineProperty(v, 'currentTime', {...})` works.\n- Adding a new media type to course assets = extend `CONTENT_TYPES` in `src/app/api/courses/[slug]/assets/[...path]/route.ts` (one map gates both the GET Content-Type header and the PUT extension allow-list). Currently supports `.png/.jpg/.jpeg/.svg/.webp/.gif/.mp4/.webm`.\n\n## 2026-05-04 00:30 - US-048\n- Implemented DataTable widget — sortable / filterable / paginated table for inline datasets, results, and comparisons. Click a column header to cycle asc → desc → unsorted (stable, original order preserved). Per-filterable-column filter row: text-contains for `string`, paired min/max number inputs for `number`. Pagination centred below the table (Prev / \"Page X of Y\" / Next) appears only when `rows.length > pageSize`. Numeric cells use `toLocaleString()` for thousand separators; boolean cells render as `✓`/`—`. Sticky `<thead>` inside an `overflow:auto` scroll wrapper (max-height 60vh) so headers stay visible when scrolling many rows.\n- Files added:\n  - `src/widgets/DataTable/{schema.ts, sample.ts, DataTableWidget.tsx, DataTableEditor.tsx}`\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/data-table.json` (regenerated by `npm run build:schemas`)\n  - `courses/datatable-test/{course.json, lessons/scores.json}` — smoke-test course (30 rows × 4 cols, pageSize 10)\n- Files changed:\n  - `src/widgets/registry.ts` — `dataTable` entry (Table icon from lucide-react, `--widget-data-table` accent), `WidgetType` union extended\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` — added `data-table` to widgets map\n  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — `DataTableSectionSchema` variant added to discriminated union\n  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — `--widget-data-table` CSS var in both light (`#4a6f8a`) + dark (`#94b3d0`) blocks\n  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — wired `DataTableEditor` into `WidgetEditPanel` and added `dataTable` body branch in `SectionRenderer`\n  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — discriminated-union case for `dataTable` + dedicated `DataTableData` schema tests, `sortRows` tests (asc/desc/unsorted/null-handling/non-mutating), `filterRows` tests (string contains, number range, AND of multiple filters, ignores non-filterable columns, empty filters pass-through)\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated\n  - `scripts/ralph/progress.txt` — added 2 codebase patterns (clampedPage instead of setState-in-effect, sticky-thead recipe)\n- Quality checks: `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm test` 7 files / 155 tests pass (added 19 new tests over US-047), `npm run lint` clean in `src/widgets/DataTable/` (only pre-existing errors remain in `claude/design/source/*.jsx` and `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/*.js`).\n- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3036/courses/datatable-test/lessons/scores, `/tmp/playwright-test-us-048.js`):\n  - Loaded 30-row × 4-col table, pageSize=10 → \"Page 1 of 3\" indicator visible.\n  - Clicked Score header → ascending sort verified (every cell ≥ previous on page 1: 20,21,23,25,26,28,30,31,33,35).\n  - Clicked again → descending sort verified (69,67,65,64,62,60,59,57,55,54).\n  - Clicked third time → header `data-sort` attribute reverts to `none` (insertion order restored).\n  - Filtered Name column with \"gra\" → summary shows \"Showing 1–1 of 1 (filtered from 30)\", only \"Grace\" visible.\n  - Cleared filter, set Score min=70 → empty state (\"No matching rows\") since sample scores top out at 69, confirming range filter applies.\n  - Clicked Next → \"Page 2 of 3\", row indices start at 10 (verified `[data-testid=\"datatable-cell-10-name\"]` exists), boolean cells render `✓`/`—`. Clicked Prev → returned to Page 1.\n  - Screenshots at `/tmp/us-048-{1-initial,2-sorted-desc,3-filtered,4-numfiltered,5-page2}.png`.\n- **Assumptions made (no human in the loop):**\n  - \"Sort indicator chevron shown next to header label\" — used `ChevronUp`/`ChevronDown` for active asc/desc and a dimmed `ChevronsUpDown` for sortable-but-unsorted columns. Non-sortable columns render as plain `<span>` with no chevron and no button.\n  - \"Numeric columns formatted via `toLocaleString()`\" applied to the user-facing cell rendering only — the underlying row data and sort comparisons use the raw numeric value, so locale-formatted strings like `1,000` don't break `min/max` filter parsing.\n  - Number range filter: blank min OR blank max means \"no bound on that side\"; setting both to blank disables the column filter entirely.\n  - Boolean column filter: AC says \"filter input per filterable column (text contains for string type, range min/max inputs for number type)\" — boolean has no described filter UI, so `filterable: true` on a boolean column degrades gracefully (the column simply renders no filter input). Sample course marks the boolean column `filterable: false` to avoid surprise.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` rule fires even when the setState is a clamping no-op like `if (page >= totalPages) setPage(totalPages-1)`. Cheaper fix than a one-shot ref: derive a `clampedPage` purely at render time and use it everywhere (slicing, indicator text, disabled-state). Saves a render cycle and silences the rule.\n  - Sticky `<thead>` works out-of-the-box with `position: sticky; top: 0` if (a) the scroll context is a wrapping `div` with `overflow: auto` and `maxHeight`, and (b) every `<th>` (or the `<thead>` itself) has an opaque `background`. Without (b), rows scroll *through* the header instead of *behind* it.\n  - For widgets that own non-trivial pure logic (sort, filter, validation), export the helpers from the schema file alongside the Zod schema so vitest can unit-test them without rendering React. `validateDragMatch` (US-047) and `sortRows`/`filterRows` (US-048) follow this pattern — keeps `schemas.test.ts` as the single test file for \"pure data\" behaviour.\n---\n\n\n## Codebase Patterns\n- Repo dir is named `US-001` (capitalized) → cannot run `create-next-app .` directly because npm rejects capital letters in package names. Workaround: scaffold into a temp dir (e.g. `/tmp/ai-lecturer-scaffold`), then copy files into the worktree (skip the inner `.git`), and set the package name in `package.json` manually.\n- `shadcn@latest` (v4.x) emits Tailwind v4 / `base-nova` style by default — incompatible with a Tailwind v3 project. Use `shadcn@2.3.0` for v3-compatible init, or write `components.json` by hand.\n- Tailwind v3 baseline = `@tailwind base; @tailwind components; @tailwind utilities;` in `globals.css` + `tailwind.config.ts` with `content: [\"./src/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,mdx}\"]` + `postcss.config.js` with `tailwindcss` and `autoprefixer` plugins. Theme/token wiring belongs in US-002, not US-001.\n- Design tokens live in `src/styles/tokens.css` (canonical source from `claude/design/source/tokens.css`) and are imported at the top of `src/app/globals.css`. Tailwind utilities resolve through CSS vars, so changing a `--*` value at runtime updates Tailwind classes too.\n- Theme/accent/density are switched by `data-theme` / `data-accent` / `data-density` attributes on `<html>` (defaults: `light` / `default` / `comfortable`). Selectors in tokens.css are scoped to `:root[data-theme=…]` etc. — adding new variants means adding a new `:root[data-…=\"…\"]` block, not a new file.\n- Geist Sans + Mono are loaded via `next/font` (`geist/font/sans`, `geist/font/mono`) in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Their `.variable` classNames define `--font-geist-sans` / `--font-geist-mono`; tokens.css references those via `var(--font-geist-sans)` inside `--font-sans` / `--font-prose` / `--font-display`. Don't hardcode font names anywhere else.\n- Playwright skill at `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/` ships without `node_modules`; run `npm install --no-audit --no-fund` inside it before first use. Its `detectDevServers()` helper missed our :3000 dev server even when up — fall back to setting `TARGET_URL` manually in the test script if detection fails.\n- **Zod is pinned to v3** (`^3.25.x`) because `zod-to-json-schema` returns an empty object on Zod v4. Don't bump zod to v4 unless the `zod-to-json-schema` import also changes. (Zod v4 has a native `z.toJSONSchema()`, but our AC mandates the third-party lib.)\n- **Vitest needs its own alias config.** `vitest.config.ts` must declare `resolve.alias = { '@': fileURLToPath(new URL('./src', import.meta.url)) }`. Vitest does NOT read `tsconfig.json#paths`. Next + `tsc` + `tsx` (used by `npm run build:schemas`) DO auto-pick it up.\n- **Eslint config does not exempt `_`-prefixed unused vars.** For \"drop one field\" test fixtures, use `const broken: Partial<typeof obj> = { ...obj }; delete broken.field;` — destructuring with `_name` triggers `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` warnings.\n- **Schema layout.** Source-of-truth Zod schemas live in two places: per-widget data shapes at `src/widgets/<Name>/schema.ts`; everything else (Course, Module, Lesson, Section discriminated union, Progress, CourseSpec) at `src/lib/schemas/`. `SectionSchema` is a `z.discriminatedUnion('type', […])` over `'theory'|'quiz'|'code'|'demo'|'sandbox'|'custom'`. Adding a new widget = new folder under `src/widgets/<Name>/` + register a variant in `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` + add it to the `widgets` map in `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts`. `npm run build:schemas` regenerates the committed `*.json` files in `src/widgets/schemas/`.\n- **Filesystem helpers** live in `src/lib/server/` (server-only — never import from a `'use client'` module). `paths.ts` exports `coursesRoot()`, `assertSafeSlug()`, `slugify()`, `courseDir/courseFile/courseSpecFile/lessonFile()`. `atomic.ts` exports `atomicWriteJson(path, data)` (writes to `<path>.tmp` then `fs.rename`). `coursesRoot()` honours `COURSES_ROOT_OVERRIDE` env var (used in tests); production reads `path.join(process.cwd(), 'courses')`. Disk layout: `courses/<slug>/{course.json, course-spec.json, lessons/<lessonSlug>.json}`.\n- **Next 16 route handlers + vitest.** Tests can import handlers directly from `src/app/api/.../route.ts` and call them with a synthesised `Request` and `{ params: Promise.resolve({...}) }` (Next 15+ wraps params in a Promise). `NextResponse.json()` returns a real `Response`, so `await res.json()` and `res.status` work in tests. Put the test file OUTSIDE `src/app/` (e.g. `src/lib/server/api.test.ts`) so Next doesn't try to compile it as a route — vitest's `include: 'src/**/*.test.ts'` still picks it up.\n- **Slug rules.** `assertSafeSlug` rejects empty strings and any slug containing `/`, `\\`, or `..` (path-traversal protection). Public slugs are derived from user input via `slugify()` (NFKD-normalise → strip combining marks → lowercase → `[_\\s]+→-` → strip non-`[a-z0-9-]` → collapse `-+` → trim). Slugify can return `''` for all-punctuation inputs; callers must guard (POST `/api/courses` returns 400 in that case).\n- **Pyodide worker singleton.** Web Workers are bundled by Turbopack via `new Worker(new URL('./worker.ts', import.meta.url))` (NO `type: 'module'` → classic worker, can use `importScripts` for CDN bootstrap). The worker file at `src/lib/pyodide/worker.ts` is excluded from main thread imports by virtue of being instantiated only via the URL constructor. Client hook lives at `src/lib/pyodide/client.ts` (`'use client'`) and exposes `usePyodide()`; the worker is a module-scope singleton created lazily on first hook subscription via `useSyncExternalStore`. Subscription on mount = lazy-load contract: dashboards / SSR never trigger worker creation. For id-keyed promise resolution: each `run`/`runWithTests` call generates `req-N`, stores `{resolve, reject}` in a `Map`, and pops on matching `event.data.id`. Custom test runner (no pytest) lives in a Python `__ai_run_tests` function injected once per worker; it `exec()`s each test body in a fresh copy of the user namespace and catches `AssertionError` separately for `assertionDetail`. Test results array shape: `[{name, passed, traceback?, assertionDetail?}]`.\n- **CodeMirror 6 setup.** Packages: `codemirror @codemirror/state @codemirror/view @codemirror/lang-python @codemirror/commands @codemirror/language @codemirror/autocomplete` (commands brings `defaultKeymap`/`history`/`historyKeymap`/`indentWithTab`; language brings `HighlightStyle`/`syntaxHighlighting`/`bracketMatching`/`indentOnInput`). Theme via `EditorView.theme({...})` consuming our `--code-bg/--code-text/--code-keyword/...` CSS vars. Highlight via `HighlightStyle.define([{ tag: t.keyword, color: 'var(--code-keyword)' }, ...])` from `@lezer/highlight` tags. Editor instantiated once in `useEffect(() => {...}, [])` with `EditorState.create({doc, extensions:[…]})`; subsequent doc updates flow via `view.dispatch({changes:{from,to,insert}})`, NOT by re-rendering. Use `EditorView.updateListener.of((u)=>u.docChanged && setCode(u.state.doc.toString()))` to mirror doc into React state.\n- **eslint react-hooks/refs rule is strict.** Never write `someRef.current = value` at component top level — must be inside `useEffect(() => { someRef.current = value; }, [value])` or inside an event handler. Pattern for \"always-fresh closure\" inside a handler set up once: declare `const valueRef = useRef(value); useEffect(() => { valueRef.current = value; }, [value]);` then read `valueRef.current` inside the long-lived closure.\n- **Cmd/Ctrl+Enter in CodeMirror.** Use `keymap.of([{ key: 'Mod-Enter', preventDefault: true, run: () => { ...; return true; } }])` and put it BEFORE the `defaultKeymap` keymap so it wins over Cm-Enter defaults. `Mod` resolves to ⌘ on Mac and Ctrl elsewhere. Have the `run` callback dispatch via a ref (`handleRunRef.current()`) so it always picks up the latest closure.\n- **Progress PATCH for sectionState.** PATCH `/api/progress` with body `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { userCode } } }`. To CLEAR a section's state (e.g. on Reset), send `{ [sectionId]: {} }` — the server's `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges into existing `sectionState[sectionId]` then replaces it, so `{}` overwrites and effectively wipes the entry's userCode. Caveat: this also wipes any sibling fields (quizSubmission) on the same section, which is fine because section IDs are per-widget-instance. To mark a section \"done\", PATCH `{ userCode, done: true }` together — `done?: boolean` is the per-section completion flag (added in US-011); sending `{ done: true }` alone would wipe userCode.\n- **CodeRunner slots (US-011).** CodeRunner exposes slot props for graded variants without re-implementing the editor/footer: `extraPanel?: ReactNode` (rendered between output panel and footer), `primaryAction?: { label, icon, onClick, disabled, variant: 'primary'|'secondary'|'ghost', testId, ariaLabel }` (replaces ▶ Run; pass `null` to hide it entirely), `onCodeChange?: (code) => void` (mirror doc into parent state), `onReset?: () => void` (parent can also reset its own state when CodeRunner's Reset fires), `outputPlaceholder?: string`. CodeRunner also exports `codeRunnerEditorTheme` and `codeRunnerHighlightStyle` so child components (e.g. inline read-only test bodies) match the editor's look. Read-only CodeMirror needs BOTH `EditorState.readOnly.of(true)` and `EditorView.editable.of(false)`.\n- **TS target ES2017.** The regex `s` (dotAll) flag triggers `TS1501`. Use `[\\s\\S]` in patterns that need to span newlines, never `/.../s`.\n- **Lesson navigation.** Flat ordered lesson list = `course.modules.flatMap(m => m.lessons)`. Prev/next of current lesson is index-1 / index+1 in that list, crossing module boundaries. Client navigation uses `router.push(\\`/courses/\\${slug}/lessons/\\${targetSlug}\\`)` from `next/navigation`'s `useRouter()`. Mark-finished is `PATCH /api/progress { courseSlug, lessonSlug, status: 'finished' }` — applyProgressPatch already handles this and stamps `finishedAt`.\n- **Adding a new widget type = 5 mandatory wiring points** (see `src/widgets/README.md`): (1) `--widget-<name>` CSS var in both light + dark blocks of `src/styles/tokens.css`; (2) Zod data schema at `src/widgets/<Name>/schema.ts` + register in `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` so `npm run build:schemas` emits `<name>.json`; (3) `widgetRegistry` entry in `src/widgets/registry.ts` (component / label / icon / accentVar) + extend the `WidgetType` union; (4) `<Name>Editor.tsx` per US-023 pattern + import + branch in both `WidgetEditPanel` and `SectionRenderer` in `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx`; (5) `<Name>SectionSchema` variant in `SectionSchema` discriminated union at `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts`. Skipping (5) means widget renders but lesson JSON containing it fails API validation. Histogram (US-030) is the canonical reference implementation.\n- **React-aware playwright slider input.** Setting `el.value` directly bypasses React's value tracker — the `onChange` handler sees the *previous* value. Use the native setter override: `Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(window.HTMLInputElement.prototype, 'value').set.call(el, '4'); el.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));`. Same pattern works for `<select>`, `<textarea>`.\n- **Pyodide lesson namespace + test isolation (US-031).** Worker holds a Python-side module-level dict `__ai_lesson_globals` (sourced from `src/lib/pyodide/runnerPython.ts` so vitest can re-install it via the `pyodide` npm dev-dep). All `'run'` calls exec'd with `runPythonAsync(code, { globals: lessonGlobalsProxy })` so the namespace persists across Code/Sandbox widgets within a lesson; `'runWithTests'` exec's user code in lessonGlobals (so helpers persist) but each test body in `dict(__ai_lesson_globals)` (so test mutations don't leak). `'resetNamespace'` (new message type, payload `{ lessonSlug }`) calls `__ai_reset_namespace()` which `.clear()`s in place — DON'T reassign the dict, the JS-side proxy points at the original object. Lesson page calls `usePyodide().resetNamespace(lessonSlug)` from a `useEffect([lessonSlug])` so the namespace wipes on every lesson navigation; toolbar `[data-testid=\"reset-session-btn\"]` exposes a manual reset with a `[data-testid=\"session-toast\"]` ack.\n- **Browser tests touching Code/Sandbox widgets must clear `~/.ai-lecturer/progress.json` per-section state first.** Persisted `userCode` (from US-011) auto-loads as `initialCode`, so a stale entry from a prior aborted run silently shapes Submit outcomes. Wipe via `node -e` JSON edit or use a throwaway course slug.\n- **CodeMirror typing in playwright auto-indents on `\\n`.** `keyboard.type('def f():\\\\n    return 42\\\\n')` produces compound indents. Use single-line lambdas where possible; otherwise insert `Enter` + `Home` between lines, or paste via `view.dispatch({changes:{...}})`.\n- **Pyodide batched stdout strips `\\n` (US-032).** `setStdout({ batched })` fires once per line, content only — never join chunks with `''` or consecutive `print()`s collapse into one line. Use the `formatStdoutChunks` helper at `src/lib/pyodide/stdout.ts`: joins with `\\n`, then per-line keeps only the substring after the last `\\r` so terminal-style in-place updates work and bare `\\r`s don't render as extra line breaks under `pre-wrap`. The CodeRunner output panel already uses `whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap'`, so once newlines actually exist in the text, multi-line output renders correctly.\n- **Worker plot capture (US-045 `runWithPlotParam`).** Matplotlib loaded lazily on first request via `loadPackage(['matplotlib'])` then `matplotlib.use('AGG')` (no display server in worker). Cache namespaces by `setupCode` STRING as the key (`__ai_pexp_namespaces[setup_code]`) so identical setupCode runs once per session — the cached dict is copied with `dict(cached)` for each render so user mutations don't leak. Capture the most-recent figure with `plt.figure(plt.get_fignums()[-1]).savefig(buf, format='png', bbox_inches='tight', dpi=110)` then `plt.close('all')` before the next render. JS plain-object payload (`{name: number|string|boolean}`) crosses the JS→Py boundary as a JsProxy → `params.to_py()` yields a Python dict; types are preserved automatically (number→float, bool→bool, string→str).\n- **Next dev (Turbopack) can hang under back-to-back playwright runs.** Symptom: first navigation succeeds, second test run's `page.goto` times out and `curl` to ANY route hangs indefinitely. Recovery: `pkill -f \"next dev\"` and restart on a different port. Suspect dangling chromium HMR socket from the previous run.\n- **react-hooks/set-state-in-effect rule.** A bare `void asyncFn()` inside `useEffect` triggers this even if setState happens after `await` (the linter doesn't follow async boundaries). Gate the call behind a one-shot `useRef(false)` flag (`if (initialRenderRef.current) return; initialRenderRef.current = true; void asyncFn();`) — the linter sees this as a one-time subscription and accepts it. Same gating pattern that GaussDemo uses with its `pendingSigmaRef` ref-check.\n- **Mark a non-Code section \"done\".** PATCH `/api/progress` with `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { done: true } } }`. `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges into `sectionState[sectionId]`, so sibling fields on other sections are untouched. Section IDs are per-widget-instance, so this is the canonical pattern when there's no `userCode` to persist (Quiz, CodeCloze, DragMatch, etc.).\n- **Mixing CSS shorthand `border` with separate `borderColor` re-renders trigger a React style warning.** Don't compose `{ border: '1px solid X' }` with a hover override `{ borderColor: 'Y' }`. Use longhand from the start (`borderWidth`, `borderStyle`, `borderColor`) so hover/feedback states only override the longhand piece. Surfaces this in DragMatch zone/bank styles where hover swaps the colour.\n- **dnd-kit (`@dnd-kit/core` + `@dnd-kit/sortable`) is already in `package.json` (added pre-MVP).** `useSensors(useSensor(PointerSensor, { activationConstraint: { distance: 4 } }), useSensor(KeyboardSensor))` is the canonical sensor set for keyboard-accessible drag widgets. `useDraggable` automatically attaches `role=\"button\"`, `tabIndex=0`, `aria-pressed`, `aria-roledescription` — verifying those attributes is enough to prove keyboard sensors are wired without simulating arrow-key navigation in playwright (each ArrowKey only moves 25 px by default and the simulated drag is brittle). For a draggable+droppable bank/zone layout: track `placement: Record<containerId, itemId[]>` with a sentinel `__bank__` id; on `onDragEnd` find the item's source container, splice it out, push into the target. Use `<DragOverlay>` so the drag preview is portal-rendered and unaffected by transforms inside the original layout.\n- **Inline syntax-highlight for cloze-style widgets.** Don't pull in CodeMirror with `Decoration.replace` widgets when the only requirement is \"syntax-highlighted Python with inline editable inputs\" — a small regex-based tokenizer (keywords / strings / comments / numbers / fn-call) inside `<pre>` is enough, and React-managed `<input>`s blur naturally without bridging CM state. CodeCloze's `tokenizePython` is the reference implementation. Use CodeMirror only when the user types into the code itself (Code, Sandbox, ParametricExplorer's Python editors).\n- **Status badge selector for browser tests.** `[data-section-id=\"<id>\"] [data-status=\"done\"]` (NOT `data-widget-status`). `StatusBadge` in `src/widgets/Widget.tsx` exposes the value via `data-status`.\n- **`type ComponentType` import for `widgetRegistry[type].component`.** When the lesson page's `SectionRenderer` forwards optional widget-specific props (e.g. `progressKey`, `onComplete`) via the registry, narrow the registry's `ComponentType<{ data?: unknown }>` with a local cast: `widgetRegistry.codeCloze.component as ComponentType<{ data?: unknown; progressKey?: typeof progressKey; onComplete?: () => void }>`. Add `type ComponentType` to the existing `from 'react'` import block in `page.tsx`.\n- **Avoid `useEffect`+`setState` for \"clamp paging index when filter shrinks rows\".** The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` rule rejects `useEffect(() => setPage(Math.max(0, totalPages-1)))`. Instead, derive a `clampedPage = Math.min(page, totalPages-1)` value during render and use it for slicing/indicator/disabled-state — let `setPage` only flip on actual user click. This keeps the linter happy and removes a redundant render cycle when filters narrow the result set.\n- **Sticky thead inside an `overflow:auto` scroll container.** `position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 1` on `<thead>` plus a non-transparent `background` on each `<th>` (or on the `<thead>` itself) is enough — no JS needed. Wrap the `<table>` in a `div` with `maxHeight: '60vh'; overflow: auto` so the sticky context is the wrapper rather than the page.\n\n## 2026-05-04 00:15 - US-047\n- Implemented DragMatch widget — drag-and-drop matching for term↔definition / category↔example / label↔diagram. Items live in a top \"bank\" droppable; zones below accept items, optionally multiple per zone with order checked. Submit highlights correct zones (--success-border + --success-subtle) and incorrect zones (--danger-border + --danger-subtle); misplaced items get a dashed danger outline plus an italic \"→ <expected zone label>\" label pointing them home. Explanation rendered below the answer area as a neutral-tone Callout (info) per the Quiz widget pattern. Section auto-marks `done` on first all-correct submission via `PATCH /api/progress`.\n- Files added:\n  - `src/widgets/DragMatch/{schema.ts, sample.ts, DragMatchWidget.tsx, DragMatchEditor.tsx}`\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/drag-match.json` (regenerated)\n  - `courses/dragmatch-test/{course.json, lessons/terms.json}` — smoke-test course\n- Files changed:","numLines":95,"startLine":42,"totalLines":212}}}
